Operator-facing text below is in Russian (standing ruling §15), with an English rendering because this session is set to English. Values in `‹…›` come from step 1's output.

## 1. Read state and evidence (Bash, foreground, read-only)

```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
W=~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
herdr agent get wgka; herdr agent get adv-fable; herdr agent get adv-codex   # state, "focused": false
herdr agent read wgka --source visible --lines 40                            # context usage
git -C $W rev-parse HEAD; git -C $W status --short
grep -rn -e '10\.77\.1\.' $W --include='*.yml' --include='*.j2' --include='*.md' | head -60
```

- If the frozen design doc already fixes the range, I relay that line to `wgka` and send no ballot.
- If `wgka` is at 50% context or more, I compact it now, while it is idle.

## 2. Write the ballot (Write tool → `$ORCH/quorum/ballot-8.md`)

```
Ballot B8 for both voting advisors. Rules: quorum/protocol.md. Read-only. Reply in English.
Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box.

B8 — wg-keepalive relay: which source range does the relay's allow-list admit?
  Context: worktree ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive, branch
  feat/wg-keepalive-relay @ ‹head SHA›; design doc ‹path:line›; plan ‹path›, step 6;
  address pools ‹file:line›; front-door allow-list ‹file:line›. Verify every statement here.
  a) 10.77.1.128/25
     Admits the WireGuard client pool only; excludes 10.77.1.0/25, which holds the OpenVPN pool.
     A second range, different from the front-door list (10.77.1.0/24).
     Cost if wrong: a legitimate source outside the /25 is dropped until the list changes.
     Rollback: one-value change, PR, redeploy.
  b) 10.77.1.0/24
     Admits the whole VPN range, WireGuard and OpenVPN pools; excludes everything outside it.
     The same range as the front-door list.
     Cost if wrong: a source inside the /24 not meant to reach the relay can reach it until the list changes.
     Rollback: one-value change, PR, redeploy.
Reply one line per ballot:  B8: <letter> — <rationale>     (or  B8: X: <proposal>)
```

## 3. Park the executor (Bash, background)

```bash
herdr agent prompt wgka "$(cat $ORCH/msg-wgka-b8.txt)" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read wgka --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $ORCH/inbox/wgka.last
```

`msg-wgka-b8.txt`:

> Your step-6 question is ballot B8, open. Your recommendation is recorded; it is not a decision. Build nothing that depends on the allow-list: no provisional value, no placeholder standing in for the choice, no test assuming either range. If plan steps exist that do not depend on step 6, carry them out under the skills in your brief, local commits only, and stop before the first step that needs the range. Otherwise change nothing. Reply in English: PARKED or steps done; branch; head SHA; test output; next step. TIME BOX 30 min.

## 4. Backlog

Edit `orchestrator/backlog.md` (blocked-on: `B8 (open)`), run `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh` in the foreground, and republish the Artifact.

## 5. Operator status (chat text, no poll)

> **Статус 01:40 — ретранслятор keepalive для WireGuard, канарейка на ccs-it**
>
> **Сейчас.** Исполнитель `wgka` остановился на шаге 6 плана: нужно выбрать, с каких адресов ретранслятор принимает keepalive-пакеты (короткие пакеты «я на связи», которые не дают VPN-туннелю закрыться) — из подсети WireGuard `10.77.1.128/25` или из всей VPN-сети `10.77.1.0/24`. Это решают два советника голосованием, бюллетень B8. Он уйдёт обоим одновременно, когда `adv-codex` закончит B7 (ревью кода): B7 ещё выполняется, результата нет. На живых машинах ничего не менялось.
>
> **Дальше.** Решение B8 → остаток плана → ревью другой моделью → моя проверка → голосования о слиянии и запуске канарейки → развёртывание на ccs-it из `main`. Время готовности назвать не могу: эти этапы ещё не пройдены. Если советники разойдутся, здесь будет ждать опрос.
>
> **От вас — одно действие руками. Это инструкция, не вопрос.**
